The code also demonstrates the use of arrays with fixed sizes for simplicity. In a production environment, you would need to implement dynamic resizing mechanisms using a memory pool manager or similar technique to handle varying data volumes efficiently.

The `add_user` and `add_transaction` functions are placeholders for adding user profiles and transactions to an account. They check if there is enough space in the respective arrays before adding new entries, ensuring that the maximum number of users and transactions per account is respected.

This code provides a foundation for further development, including more complex data structures, error handling, memory management optimizations, and additional features as specified in the task description."]

