This code snippet demonstrates how to create a dynamic linked list of `record` structures in C. Each record contains an integer value and a pointer to the next record in the list. The `create_record` function allocates memory for a new record, initializes its fields, and returns a pointer to the new record. The `add_record_to_list` function adds a new record to the beginning of the linked list. The `generate_random_value` function generates a random integer within a specified range using the NRNG (pseudo-random number generator). The `populate_list_with_random_values` function populates the linked list with a specified number of records, each containing a random value. Finally, the `free_record` function recursively deallocates all memory used by the linked list to prevent memory leaks.']
